  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Hassett described working groups considering how AI can make both workers and firms more productive and referred to an unprecedented productivity boom. He said firms are finding AI makes workers productive enough that they do not necessarily need to hire new college graduates. He described AI-related risks as solvable problems and said the private sector is the right place to solve them. In May 2026, he said a possible executive order was being studied to provide a clear road map.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
   "sentences": [
